  "reason": "The records jointly make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. R1, R9, and especially R14 establish SPS near 1000 °C in compositionally similar multicomponent alloys, with R9 showing a dense, pore-free structure and R14 directly linking temperature to diffusion-driven densification. R11 and R13 show that mechanically alloyed BCC powders can decompose or precipitate secondary phases during SPS, including oxide-related strengthening. Independently, R5, R6, R7, R15, R16, and R18 establish that dense, continuous oxide or passive films suppress ionic or oxygen transport and improve corrosion or oxidation resistance, while insufficiently dense films fail. An expert could therefore propose SPS around 1000 °C to combine densification, thermally activated precipitation, and protective-film formation, although the exact AlV2O4, FeAl2O4, and FeTiO3 phase identities and the precise optimum properties are not disclosed."
